# Trivy ignore file for false positives and accepted risks
# Documentation: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
#
# CVE EXPIRATION TRACKING
# =======================
# Each CVE entry must include a REVIEW BY date in the comment format:
#   # CVE-XXXX-YYYY - Description (REVIEW BY: YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# A CI check validates that no CVE review dates have expired.
# See scripts/check-trivyignore-expiry.sh for the validation script.
#
# Review guidelines:
# - New CVEs: Set review date 3-6 months from date of addition
# - On review: Check if fix is available, reassess risk, extend or remove
# - Remove entries when fixes become available

# =============================================================================
# Alpine Linux Base Image
# =============================================================================
# (no active entries since the 2026-10-04 sweep: the two BusyBox ignores were
# dead — the frontend image ships busybox 1.37.0-r31, past the Alpine secdb
# fixes 1.37.0-r24 / 1.37.0-r27, so Trivy no longer reports them. The frontend
# scan runs ignore-unfixed FALSE and showed zero BusyBox rows. See REMOVED.)

# =============================================================================
# Debian/Ubuntu Base Image - No Fix Available
# =============================================================================
# These CVEs are in system packages with no upstream fix available

# NOTE (sweep 2026-10-04): the 2026-09-16 NOTE below was kept but is now
# EXECUTED. Every entry the Debian tracker marks "resolved" with the fix in the
# archive has been DELETED on image evidence, not assumption: the amd64 CI
# install log (run 37208159907 @ 6b33a2af) and the base image's own dpkg status
# show the installed version at/above each fixed version — libzvbi u1,
# libglib2.0 u9, gdk-pixbuf u4, libssh u2, pam u2, glibc u14, libpng u5, gpgv
# u2. What remains in this section is ONLY what the tracker still marks
# "open" (re-verified 2026-10-04) or that is not in the runtime image at all.
# The two prod stages also changed: backend apt --only-upgrade now names
# libpcre2-8-0 (the one real move — a base-owned package, where an old digest
# or cached layer IS the rollback vector) plus the base-owned fixed set
# (libc6/libc-bin, libpam*, gpgv) as a guard against exactly that; the
# ffmpeg-closure names there run empty by construction (this same RUN installs
# them from current lists). frontend apk upgrade --no-cache pcre2 does the
# Alpine half. See each Dockerfile's comment for the measured split.
# Guard: backend/tests/unit/scripts/test_backend_image_trivy_clean.py
#
# NOTE (review 2026-09-16, historical): the Debian security tracker showed fix
# versions in bookworm point releases for several entries then listed (e.g.
# libsqlite3 3.40.1-2+deb12u2, libpng 1.6.39-2+deb12u2, libzvbi
# 0.2.41-1+deb12u1, glibc 2.36-9+deb12u14). They stayed pending image-proof;
# the 2026-10-04 sweep gathered it (and note libsqlite3 turned out to be
# tracker-OPEN — that entry was corrected, not deleted).

# CVE-2023-6879 - libaom heap-buffer-overflow CRITICAL (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-05)
# No fix in Debian stable
# Affects AV1 codec library used by ffmpeg, not directly used by application
CVE-2023-6879

# CVE-2023-39616 - libaom invalid read (REVIEW BY: 2027-06-05)
# Marked "will_not_fix" by Debian
# Same package as above, AV1 codec not directly used
CVE-2023-39616

# CVE-2023-45221 - libmfx improper buffer restrictions (REVIEW BY: 2027-06-05)
# Marked "will_not_fix" by Debian
# Intel Media SDK not used by our application
CVE-2023-45221

# CVE-2023-52355 - libtiff heap buffer overflow (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-05)
# Affected status
# TIFF processing handled by PIL with memory safety measures
CVE-2023-52355

# CVE-2023-25193 - libharfbuzz O(n^2) complexity (REVIEW BY: 2027-06-05)
# No fix available
# Text shaping library, DoS risk only in malicious font processing
CVE-2023-25193

# CVE-2024-23775 - libmbedcrypto integer overflow (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-05)
# No fix in Debian stable
# Used by some Python SSL, but not critical path
CVE-2024-23775

# CVE-2025-47917 - libmbedcrypto use-after-free CRITICAL (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-05)
# Tracker: still (unfixed) on bookworm (verified 2026-09-16)
# Mbed TLS library used by librist (RIST protocol), ffmpeg dependency
CVE-2025-47917

# CVE-2025-48965 - libmbedcrypto NULL pointer dereference (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-05)
# Tracker status OPEN on bookworm — no fix version exists (re-verified
# 2026-10-04). An earlier note here cited 2.28.3-1 as a fix release; it is not —
# that is simply the CURRENT published version. Do not hunt for a point release;
# there is none.
# Mbed TLS library used by librist (RIST protocol), ffmpeg dependency
CVE-2025-48965

# CVE-2025-52496 - libmbedcrypto AESNI race condition (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-05)
# Tracker status OPEN on bookworm — no fix version exists (re-verified
# 2026-10-04); same corrected entry as CVE-2025-48965 above.
# Mbed TLS library used by librist (RIST protocol), ffmpeg dependency
CVE-2025-52496

# CVE-2025-7458 - libsqlite3-0 integer overflow CRITICAL (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-05)
# Tracker status OPEN on bookworm — no fix version exists (re-verified
# 2026-10-04). The 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 cited by the 2026-09-16 review is the
# CURRENT published version (the base image installs exactly it), not a fix —
# the entry is a genuine no-fix risk, not a pending deletion.
# SQLite vulnerability, affects libsqlite3-0 package used by Python stdlib
CVE-2025-7458

# CVE-2023-2953 - OpenLDAP null pointer dereference in ber_memalloc_x (REVIEW BY: 2027-04-21)
# HIGH severity, no DSA for bookworm (tracker <no-dsa>, verified 2026-09-16)
# Affects libldap-2.5-0 package, a transitive dependency of curl (via libcurl4)
# Not exploitable in our context:
#   1. Our application does not use LDAP functionality
#   2. libldap is only included as a dependency of curl, used for health checks
#   3. The vulnerability requires LDAP operations to trigger
# Reference: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-2953
CVE-2023-2953

# =============================================================================
# Python Package Vulnerabilities - No Fix Available
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2024-23342 - python-ecdsa Minerva timing attack (REVIEW BY: 2027-05-03)
# HIGH severity, no fix planned by upstream maintainer (OSV: unfixed at the
# locked ecdsa 0.19.2, re-verified 2026-09-16)
# python-ecdsa project considers side-channel attacks out of scope
# ecdsa is a transitive dependency via python-jose (JWT library)
# Not exploitable in our context:
#   1. JWT signing uses HMAC (HS256), not ECDSA in our implementation
#   2. Timing attack requires local timing measurement capability
#   3. No ECDH operations or ECDSA signing in production code paths
CVE-2024-23342

