# =============================================================================
# pip's VENDORED bundle (backend image scan, added 2026-09-20)
# =============================================================================
# These two are not installed packages and are not importable by the app. They
# are private copies inside pip's own _vendor/ tree in the base image
# (python:3.14-slim-bookworm ships pip 26.2.1). Trivy reads their versions from
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt and pip's shipped bom.cdx.json, which is why they have
# no .dist-info and report under a bare "Python" target with no path.
#
# Verified 2026-09-20 by listing the built image (run 35550126923, backend image
# scan diagnostic). The ONLY python dist-info present are:
#     /app/.venv/.../msgpack-1.2.2.dist-info      (clean)
#     /app/.venv/.../setuptools-84.0.0.dist-info  (clean)
# uv.lock pins msgpack 1.2.2 and setuptools 84.0.0, so our dependency graph is
# already past both fixes. Only upstream pip can revendor its bundle; there is
# no action available to this repo short of removing pip from the image.
#
# ignore-unfixed does NOT filter these: a fix exists upstream (1.2.1 / 78.1.1),
# it is simply not ours to apply. Re-check when the base image ships a newer pip.
#
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 - msgpack 1.1.2 vendored in pip/_vendor (REVIEW BY: 2026-12-20)
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
# CVE-2025-47273 - setuptools 70.3.0 vendored in pip/_vendor (REVIEW BY: 2026-12-20)
CVE-2025-47273

# 2026-10-01 addendum, same class (ledger row 66, branch
# chore/main-green-trivy-allowlist): the f9778503 scan
# added two HIGH urllib3 findings installed "2.7.0" fixed "2.8.0" under the
# bare "Python" target. NOT the app's urllib3 — the venv scanned
# urllib3-2.8.0.dist-info with ZERO findings (uv.lock pins 2.8.0; the build
# log line "+ urllib3==2.8.0" confirms what uv sync installed). The 2.7.0
# pair is pip's vendored copy again: pip/_vendor/vendor.txt in the pip
# 26.2.1 wheel reads "urllib3==2.7.0" (verified 2026-10-01 by downloading
# pip==26.2.1 --no-deps and unzipping the wheel). Only upstream pip can
# revendor; re-check when the base image ships a newer pip.
#
# CVE-2026-97687 - urllib3 2.7.0 vendored in pip/_vendor (REVIEW BY: 2026-12-20)
CVE-2026-97687
# CVE-2026-97689 - urllib3 2.7.0 vendored in pip/_vendor (REVIEW BY: 2026-12-20)
CVE-2026-97689

# =============================================================================
# Frontend npm dependencies (filesystem scan of frontend/package-lock.json and bun.lock)
# =============================================================================
# braces 3.0.3 is the newest release published to npm (2024-09-18; `npm view braces
# versions` ends at 3.0.3, read 2026-10-03), so no fixed version exists to upgrade to.
# It is reached through tailwindcss (build-time CSS generation) via chokidar, micromatch
# and fast-glob. The production image copies only /app/dist into nginx
# (frontend/Dockerfile:127), so braces is not in the runtime image, and the advisory
# (stack overflow on deeply nested brace patterns) needs an attacker-controlled pattern
# handed to braces. Re-check when braces publishes a release or tailwindcss stops using it.
#
# CVE-2026-93687 - braces 3.0.3 stack overflow on deeply nested patterns, via tailwindcss (REVIEW BY: 2027-01-03)
CVE-2026-93687
